<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104723" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐάζω</span></b>  (pres. only in compd.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-</span>), aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτρίασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theo Sm.
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐάσσω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				765.37
			</span></i>, 
				Att.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριάττω</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i>:—<i>conquer, vanquish,</i> properly of a
			wrestler, who did not win until <i>he had thrice thrown</i> his
			adversary, or conquered him <i>in three bouts</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλαίσματα</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τριαχθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thugen.
					1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> (Hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριακτήρ, ἀτρίακτος,
				ἀποτριάζω.</span>) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>multiply by three,</i> Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.29
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.60
			</span></i> P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
